    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=CURRENT TRAFFIC VALUE SELECTION RULES\n\nThe workflow can be triggered by either Webhook or Webhook1.\nOnly one webhook will be executed for a given workflow execution.\n\nYou MUST first determine which webhook has been executed.\n\nIMPORTANT:\nNever attempt to read data from an unexecuted webhook.\nNever combine values from Webhook and Webhook1.\n\n1. AVERAGE SPEED\n\nIf Webhook has been executed:\n    Use the average_speed value received from the executed Webhook as the current average speed.\n\nIf Webhook has NOT been executed:\n    Calculate the average speed using the previous traffic readings provided in the historical traffic data.\n\nUse the relevant previous historical records for the same road and similar time period.\n\nDo not use a fixed speed threshold.\n\n2. VEHICLE COUNT\n\nIf Webhook has been executed:\n    Use the vehicle_count value received from the executed Webhook as the current vehicle count.\n\nIf Webhook has NOT been executed:\n    Calculate the average vehicle count using the previous traffic readings provided in the historical traffic data.\n\nUse the relevant previous historical records for the same road and similar time period.\n\nDo not use a fixed vehicle-count threshold.\n\n3. TEMPERATURE\n\nIf Webhook has been executed:\n    Use the temperature value received from the executed Webhook.\n\nIf Webhook has NOT been executed:\n    Find the historical traffic record that is approximately 5 minutes before the current requested date and time.\n\nUse the temperature from that historical record as the current temperature.\n\nDo not calculate or average the temperature.\n\nDo not estimate the temperature.\n\nIf an exact 5-minute historical record is unavailable, use the closest available historical record before the requested time.\n\n4. HUMIDITY\n\nIf Webhook has been executed:\n    Use the humidity value received from the executed Webhook.\n\nIf Webhook has NOT been executed:\n    Find the historical traffic record that is approximately 5 minutes before the current requested date and time.\n\nUse the humidity from that historical record as the current humidity.\n\nDo not calculate or average the humidity.\n\nDo not estimate the humidity.\n\nIf an exact 5-minute historical record is unavailable, use the closest available historical record before the requested time.\n\n\nIMPORTANT DATA RULES\n\nThe historical data is provided below:\n\n{{ JSON.stringify($json?.traffic_data || []) }}\n\nWhen calculating fallback values:\n\n- Use only historical records for the same road.\n- Prefer records closest to the requested time.\n- Prefer records from the same day when available.\n- Do not use unrelated roads.\n- Do not invent missing values.\n- Do not use arbitrary fixed thresholds.\n- Do not mix current Webhook values with fallback historical values unnecessarily.\n\n\nFINAL CURRENT VALUES\n\nAfter applying the rules above, determine exactly one value for each:\n\nroad\naverage_speed\nvehicle_count\nrecorded_date\nrecorded_time\ntemperature\nhumidity\n\nThese values will be used as the CURRENT TRAFFIC values for the analysis.\n\nThen perform the traffic-congestion analysis using these selected current values against all relevant historical traffic data.\n\nThe conjestion should be in the form YES or NO.",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "You are an AI Traffic Management Analyst.\n\nYour primary responsibility is to analyze current traffic data against all relevant historical traffic data and determine whether the current situation requires traffic-management attention.\n\nYou have access to a Gmail tool.\n\nIMPORTANT TOOL-USAGE RULE:\n\nYou, the AI Agent, are solely responsible for deciding whether an email should be sent.\n\nDo NOT send an email for every analysis.\n\nDo NOT call the Gmail tool automatically.\n\nFirst complete the entire traffic analysis.\n\nThen make ONE decision:\n\n1. If the final severity is LOW or MEDIUM:\n   - Do NOT call Gmail.\n   - Do not send any email.\n\n2. If the final severity is HIGH or EXTREME:\n   - Call Gmail exactly ONCE.\n   - Send exactly ONE email.\n   - Do not call Gmail again for the same analysis.\n\nThere must never be more than one Gmail call during a single workflow execution.\n\nThe Gmail tool must only be called after the complete traffic analysis has been completed.\n\nIf Gmail is not required, simply return the structured traffic analysis without calling Gmail.\n\nThe Gmail tool is NOT a mandatory step.\n\nYou must decide whether Gmail is necessary based on the complete traffic analysis, not merely because the tool is available."
        }
      },
